## 6. Verdict on scope (as hypothesised by idea-repo, not yet a plan assessment)

The minimum credible scope — linear/deep-linear JEPA on synthetic data (quantitative tests) plus
small nonlinear JEPAs on CIFAR-10/MNIST (qualitative tests), all three heuristics — is **feasible on
this world's compute within a few turns of wall-clock**, provided the nonlinear grid is bounded
(~≤100 runs at the workhorse scale) and runs as `local-compute` jobs rather than in-turn waits.
ImageNet-scale or larger models are infeasible and must stay out of the plan.
